{"response": "Probably compatible

The 2018 *Der Nervenarzt* review classified levetiracetam as “probably compatible” with breastfeeding. This is the review authors’ historical classification, not an individualized medication decision. [PubMed abstract](https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/29487964/)

Informational only; not medical advice. Compiled from public NIH/NLM/FDA data, which may be incomplete or out of date. Patients should talk to a clinician, pharmacist or poison control before starting, stopping or changing any medication."}

{"response": "Placebo

ClinicalTrials.gov lists nifedipine and “Placebo of Nifedipine” as the interventions for the 48-hour PPROM tocolysis study (NCT03976063): https://clinicaltrials.gov/study/NCT03976063. Its status is **ACTIVE_NOT_RECRUITING**; registration describes the study design and does **not** establish treatment benefit.

